      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A general somatic syndromal approach to evaluation of clinical status by SAPS II and APACH II scores was used in 41 patients operated on for gastric cancer. Epidural analgesia in these patients promoted rapid regression of the severity of condition, did not require high opioid doses, had a positive effect on the peristaltic activity of the intestine, and accelerated treatment in intensive care wards."},
